@startuml scenario-roaming-full
' =====================================================================
'  FULL SCENARIO — Roaming Analysis Service
'  End-to-end analyst workflow: morning check → anomaly investigation
'  → SLA breach → agreement renegotiation → synthetic tests → forecast.
'  Covers every endpoint of RoamingController (18 operations).
' =====================================================================

title Full Scenario — Roaming Analysis Service\n"A Security Analyst's Morning Shift on the Nexo 5GC Platform"

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderThickness 1.5
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor transparent
skinparam participantBorderColor #444444
skinparam actorBorderColor #444444

actor       "Security Analyst\n(analyst-user)" as ANALYST
participant "Angular SPA\n:4200"               as SPA
participant "API Gateway\n:9000"               as GW
participant "Keycloak\n:8081"                  as KC
participant "RoamingController\n:9002"         as CTL
participant "RoamingAnalysisService"           as RAS
participant "RoamingInsightsService"           as RIS
participant "PerformanceAssuranceService"      as PAS
participant "AnomalyDetector"                  as AD
participant "RiskAnalyzer"                     as RA
participant "KpiCalculator"                    as KPI
participant "RoamingSimulator"                 as SIM
database    "roaming-mysql\n:3307"             as DB
database    "Grafana\n:3000"                   as GRAF

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 0 — Context
' =====================================================================
note over ANALYST, DB #FEF7E0
  **Business context**
  Home network: Nexo (operators OPRITWND · OPRGBEE · OPRESORE)
  ~20 partner PLMNs worldwide (UK, France, Germany, USA, India, Nigeria…)
  CDR + attach-event + session-QoS data loaded from CSV at startup.
  RoamingAgreementSeeder created one IR.21 agreement per partner with SLA thresholds.
  Streaming tick runs every 5 min, folding FIVE_MIN windows into rolling performance scores.
end note

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 1 — Authentication
' =====================================================================
== Phase 1 · Authentication ==

ANALYST -> SPA : Login (analyst-user / password)
SPA -> GW : POST /api/auth/login
GW -> KC  : password grant\nclient_id=platform-client\nusername=analyst-user
KC --> GW : access_token (JWT)\nroles: [SECURITY_ANALYST]\npermissions: [PERM_roaming-events:read]
GW --> SPA : 200 { access_token, expires_in }
SPA --> ANALYST : Security Analyst console unlocked\n(Roaming dashboard tab visible)

note right of KC
  SECURITY_ANALYST composite role
  expands to PERM_roaming-events:read.
  Gateway validates JWKS on every request.
  Service also validates with @PreAuthorize.
  Defence-in-depth: two enforcement points.
end note

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 2 — Morning Dashboard Check
' =====================================================================
== Phase 2 · Morning Dashboard Check ==

ANALYST -> SPA : Open "Roaming Live Monitor"

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/live?windowMinutes=60\nAuthorization: Bearer <JWT>
GW  -> CTL : forward (PERM_roaming-events:read ✓)
CTL -> RIS : live(60)
RIS -> DB  : SELECT roaming_events WHERE timestamp >= now-60min
DB  --> RIS : List<RoamingEvent> (window)
RIS -> RA  : score(event) × N
RA  --> RIS : risk scores (0-100 additive heuristic)
RIS --> CTL : LiveMonitorDto\n{ events:14, subscribers:8 420, rate:0.23/min,\n  avgRisk:41, highRisk:3, revenueEur:12 840 }
CTL --> GW  : 200 JSON
GW  --> SPA : LiveMonitorDto
SPA --> ANALYST : Live dashboard:\n3 HIGH-risk events in last hour ⚠️\nRevenue: €12 840

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 3 — Event List & Filtering
' =====================================================================
== Phase 3 · Event Filtering ==

ANALYST -> SPA : Filter: Direction=INBOUND · Risk=HIGH

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/events?direction=INBOUND&riskLevel=HIGH
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> RAS : listEvents(INBOUND, null, HIGH)
RAS -> DB  : SELECT roaming_events (full table via projection)
DB  --> RAS : all events
RAS -> RA  : score(e) per event → filter HIGH (score≥60)
RA  --> RAS : scored events
RAS --> CTL : [RE-1002 USA 310-260 · RE-1006 India 404-45 · RE-1008 Nigeria 621-30]
CTL --> GW  : 200 JSON
GW  --> SPA : 3 HIGH-risk inbound events

ANALYST -> SPA : Click event RE-1002 (USA)

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/events/RE-1002
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> RAS : getEvent("RE-1002")
RAS -> DB  : SELECT WHERE id='RE-1002'
DB  --> RAS : RoamingEvent { plmn:310-260, country:USA,\n  subscribers:12, errors:9, newDeviceRatio:0.55,\n  impossibleTravel:true, latency:98ms, drop:14.7% }
RAS -> RA   : score → 82 (HIGH)
RAS --> CTL : RoamingEventDto (riskScore=82, riskLevel=HIGH)
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : Event detail panel
SPA --> ANALYST : ⚠ RE-1002 — USA 310-260\nriskScore=82 HIGH\nImpossible travel detected · 9 signalling errors\n55% new-device ratio

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 4 — Anomaly Engine
' =====================================================================
== Phase 4 · Anomaly Detection Engine ==

ANALYST -> SPA : Open "Anomaly Detection" tab

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/anomalies
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> RIS : anomalies()
RIS -> AD  : detect(allEvents)

loop for each event in population
  AD -> RA  : score(event)
  RA --> AD : riskScore
  AD -> AD  : compute population mean & std-dev\nz-score = (score - mean) / std\ncomposite = ½·risk + capped z-score deviations\n+25 bonus if impossibleTravel=true
end

AD --> RIS : List<AnomalyDto>\n[{id:RE-1002, score:88, deviation:+3.2σ,\n  severity:CRITICAL,\n  reasons:[impossible_travel, high_new_device_ratio, signalling_errors]},\n {id:RE-1008, score:74, deviation:+2.1σ,\n  severity:HIGH,\n  reasons:[impossible_travel, latency_spike]},\n {id:RE-1006, score:61, deviation:+1.4σ,\n  severity:MEDIUM,\n  reasons:[high_new_device_ratio]}]
RIS --> CTL : 3 anomalies
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : anomaly list
SPA --> ANALYST : 🚨 RE-1002 CRITICAL  (+3.2σ) — impossible travel + fraud signals\n⚠ RE-1008 HIGH     (+2.1σ) — Nigeria: impossible travel + latency\n▲ RE-1006 MEDIUM   (+1.4σ) — India: 42% new-device ratio

note over AD
  AnomalyDetector is the clean seam for ML (ADR-02).
  Currently: statistical (z-score) + rule-based (heuristic).
  Same detector reused for /upload CSV and /simulate batch.
end note

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 5 — Partner Roll-up
' =====================================================================
== Phase 5 · Partner Analytics ==

ANALYST -> SPA : Open "Partners" panel

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/partners
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> RAS : partners()
RAS -> DB  : SELECT all events
DB  --> RAS : all
RAS -> RA  : score per event → group by partnerPlmn\navg risk, peak risk, highRisk count
RAS --> CTL : List<PartnerSummaryDto> (ordered worst→best avg risk)\n[{310-260 USA  avgRisk:82 peakRisk:HIGH  events:2},\n {621-30  Nigeria avgRisk:71 peakRisk:HIGH  events:1},\n {404-45  India  avgRisk:61 peakRisk:HIGH  events:1},\n ...]
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : partner table
SPA --> ANALYST : 📊 3 partners flagged HIGH\nUSA 310-260 worst average risk (82)

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 6 — Platform Summary for Dashboard
' =====================================================================
== Phase 6 · Dashboard Summary ==

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/summary
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> RAS : summary()
RAS -> DB  : SELECT all events
DB  --> RAS : all events (sorted by hour)
RAS --> CTL : RoamingSummaryDto\n{ total:12, totalSubs:6 802, inbound:8, outbound:4,\n  byRisk:{LOW:5,MEDIUM:4,HIGH:3}, highRisk:3,\n  volumeSeries:[{08:00,1420},{09:00,2310},…] }
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : summary
SPA --> ANALYST : Dashboard filled — volume chart, risk donut, direction split

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 7 — CSV Upload (New CDR Batch from NOC)
' =====================================================================
== Phase 7 · CSV Upload Analysis (NOC CDR Batch) ==

note over ANALYST #FFF3E0
  The NOC exports a new CDR CSV every morning.
  The analyst uploads it for instant analysis without touching production data.
end note

ANALYST -> SPA : Upload cdrs-2026-09-10.csv (7 MB)

SPA -> GW  : POST /api/roaming/upload?hoursAhead=6\nContent-Type: multipart/form-data\nfile=cdrs-2026-09-10.csv
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> RIS : analyzeCsv(file, 6)
RIS -> RIS : CsvParser.parse(file)\n→ { parsed:342, skipped:4, events:342 }
RIS -> RAS : summary(csvEvents)
RAS --> RIS : RoamingSummaryDto (CSV-scoped)
RIS -> AD  : detect(csvEvents)
AD  --> RIS : 11 anomalies in batch
RIS -> RIS  : forecast(6, csvEvents)\nlinear-regression over hourly buckets
RIS --> CTL : CsvAnalysisDto\n{ fileName:cdrs-2026-09-10.csv, parsed:342, skipped:4,\n  summary:{total:342, highRisk:11},\n  anomalies:[11 flagged],\n  forecast:[{14:00,1820},{15:00,2140},{16:00,2390},...] }
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : CsvAnalysisDto
SPA --> ANALYST : 📂 Batch analysed: 342 events · 11 anomalies\nForecast: traffic peaks at 2 390 subs by 16:00

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 8 — Performance Assurance KPIs
' =====================================================================
== Phase 8 · Performance Assurance KPIs ==

ANALYST -> SPA : KPI tab → window=DAY · all partners

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/kpis?window=DAY
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> PAS : kpis(null, DAY)
PAS -> DB  : findInWindow(start=today-00:00, end=now)\n  AttachEvents · RoamingCDRs · SessionQoS
DB  --> PAS : raw signalling records
PAS -> KPI : compute(ALL, DAY, attaches, cdrs, sessions)
KPI --> PAS : KpiSetDto\n{ registrationSuccessRate:97.3%, asr:72.4%, ner:88.1%,\n  sessionSetupSuccessRate:98.1%, acd:142s,\n  latencyP50:41ms, latencyP95:108ms, latencyP99:187ms,\n  dropRatePct:1.8%, throughputMbps:38.4 }
PAS --> CTL : KpiSetDto
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : KPIs
SPA --> ANALYST : ✅ Registration: 97.3%  ASR: 72.4%  Latency P95: 108ms\n⚠ latencyP95 approaching SLA limit for 2 partners

ANALYST -> SPA : KPI Timeseries — last 12 DAY windows

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/kpis/timeseries?window=DAY&count=12
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> PAS : timeseries(null, DAY, 12)

loop 12 times (oldest → newest)
  PAS -> KPI : computeWindow(partner=ALL, window, start, end)
  KPI --> PAS : KpiSetDto
end

PAS --> CTL : KpiTimeseriesDto { 12 points }
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : timeseries
SPA --> ANALYST : 📈 12-day trend chart — ASR degrading -4% over last 3 days

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 9 — SLA Evaluation
' =====================================================================
== Phase 9 · SLA Breach Evaluation ==

ANALYST -> SPA : Open "SLA Compliance" view

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/sla?window=DAY
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> PAS : evaluateSla(DAY)

loop for each RoamingAgreement
  PAS -> PAS : timeseries(partner, DAY, lookback=3 windows)
  PAS -> PAS : breaches(latestWindow, agreement)
  PAS -> PAS : consecutiveBreach count\nalarm = consecutive ≥ 3
end

PAS --> CTL : List<SlaEvaluationDto> sorted worst-first\n[{partner:310-260 USA,\n  breaches:[ASR 58.1% < 60%, latencyP95 134ms > 120ms],\n  consecutive:3, alarm:TRUE, rollingScore:61.2, tier:WATCH},\n {partner:621-30 Nigeria,\n  breaches:[dropRate 4.1% > 3%],\n  consecutive:1, alarm:false, rollingScore:74.5, tier:STANDARD},\n ...10 compliant partners]
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : SLA results
SPA --> ANALYST : 🚨 ALARM — USA 310-260: 3 consecutive DAY windows breached\n  ASR below minimum (58.1% < 60%)\n  Latency P95 exceeded (134ms > 120ms)\n⚠ Nigeria 621-30: single breach, drop rate (4.1%)

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 10 — Agreements & Optimization
' =====================================================================
== Phase 10 · Agreement Optimization ==

ANALYST -> SPA : View agreements list

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/agreements
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> PAS : agreements()
PAS -> DB  : SELECT roaming_agreements
DB  --> PAS : List<RoamingAgreement>\n(IR.21 refs, SLA thresholds, rolling scores, tiers)
PAS --> CTL : List<AgreementDto>
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : all agreements
SPA --> ANALYST : 20 agreements displayed with SLA thresholds and tiers

ANALYST -> SPA : Open "Agreement Optimization" panel

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/optimization
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> RIS : optimization()
RIS -> DB  : all events
DB  --> RIS : grouped by PLMN
RIS -> RA  : avgRisk per partner
RA  --> RIS : risk scores
RIS -> RIS  : per partner: revenue · cost · margin · QoS experience\n→ RENEGOTIATE if margin<0\n→ MONITOR if avgRisk≥60\n→ IMPROVE_QOS if experience<50\n→ PREFERRED if margin≥40% & risk<30\n→ STEADY otherwise
RIS --> CTL : List<OptimizationDto> sorted by margin desc\n[{310-260 USA,  action:MONITOR,\n  revenue:€84, cost:€62, margin:€22, marginPct:26%,\n  rec:"Profitable but high fraud — tighten steering"},\n {621-30 Nigeria, action:RENEGOTIATE,\n  revenue:€38, cost:€51, margin:€-13,\n  rec:"Loss-making — renegotiate or introduce data caps"},\n {208-10 France,  action:PREFERRED,\n  revenue:€420, margin:44%, rec:"High-margin low-risk — preferred partner"},\n ...]
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : optimization list
SPA --> ANALYST : 💰 France 208-10 → PREFERRED (€420 revenue, 44% margin)\n📊 USA 310-260 → MONITOR (high fraud, profitable)\n❌ Nigeria 621-30 → RENEGOTIATE (loss-making, −€13)

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 11 — Revenue & QoS Overview
' =====================================================================
== Phase 11 · Revenue & QoS Overview ==

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/revenue
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> RIS : revenue()
RIS -> DB  : all events
DB  --> RIS : sum revenue / cost per direction
RIS --> CTL : RevenueDto\n{ totalRevenue:€4 820, cost:€3 140, margin:€1 680,\n  marginPct:34.8%, perSubscriberRevenue:€0.71,\n  inbound:€3 210, outbound:€1 610,\n  top5:[{France:€420},{UK:€380},{Germany:€290},...] }
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : RevenueDto
SPA --> ANALYST : 📊 Total margin: €1 680 (34.8%)\nTop earner: France 208-10

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/qos
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> RIS : qos()
RIS -> RIS  : avg latency / throughput / drop over all events\n→ QoS score 0-100 (penalise latency>40ms, drop, low throughput)
RIS --> CTL : QosDto\n{ avgLatencyMs:52.3, avgThroughputMbps:36.1,\n  avgDropPct:2.1, qosScore:71,\n  worst3:[{Nigeria:score18,Poor},{USA:score32,Poor},{India:score44,Fair}] }
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : QosDto
SPA --> ANALYST : 📡 Platform QoS score: 71/100\n⚠ Nigeria (18 · Poor) · USA (32 · Poor) worst performers

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/experience
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> RIS : experience()
RIS --> CTL : List<ExperienceDto> worst-first\n(latency · throughput · drop · experienceScore · rating per PLMN)
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : per-partner experience scores
SPA --> ANALYST : Customer experience table sorted worst → best

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 12 — Synthetic IREG Test Calls
' =====================================================================
== Phase 12 · Synthetic Test Calls (IREG-style probe) ==

note over ANALYST #FEF7E0
  Before escalating to the partner NOC about USA 310-260,
  the analyst triggers synthetic test transactions to confirm degradation.
end note

ANALYST -> SPA : Run synthetic test-calls

SPA -> GW  : POST /api/roaming/test-calls/run
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> PAS : runSyntheticTests()

loop for each active agreement × each TXN_TYPE [REGISTRATION, MO_CALL, MT_CALL, SMS, DATA_SESSION]
  PAS -> PAS : health = max(0.5, rollingScore/100)\npass = random() < health\nlatency = random(20..200 ms)
end

PAS --> CTL : List<SyntheticTestResultDto>\n[{310-260, REGISTRATION, FAIL, 178ms, "timeout/no response"},\n {310-260, MO_CALL,      FAIL, 192ms, "timeout/no response"},\n {310-260, SMS,         PASS, 47ms,  "OK"},\n {208-10, REGISTRATION, PASS, 23ms,  "OK"}, ...]
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : test results
SPA --> ANALYST : 🧪 USA 310-260: REGISTRATION FAIL · MO_CALL FAIL (health=61%)\n✅ France 208-10: all 5 transaction types PASSED\n→ Confirmed: USA partner degraded. Escalate to NOC.

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 13 — Traffic Simulation (Validate Anomaly Pipeline)
' =====================================================================
== Phase 13 · Traffic Simulation ==

note over ANALYST #E8F0FE
  Before end-of-shift, the analyst runs a simulation to verify the
  anomaly detection pipeline will react to a spike in high-risk traffic.
end note

ANALYST -> SPA : Simulate 30 events over 120 min window

SPA -> GW  : POST /api/roaming/simulate?count=30&minutesSpread=120&windowMinutes=60
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> RIS : simulate(30, 120, 60)
RIS -> SIM : generate(30, 120, synthetic=false)

loop 30 events (SIM-prefixed ids)
  SIM -> SIM : random direction · PLMN · country · subscribers\n  derive QoS + commercial figures\n  persist to roaming_events table
end

SIM --> RIS : 30 generated events
RIS -> RIS  : liveOver(generated, windowMinutes=60)
RIS --> CTL : SimulationResultDto\n{ generated:30, windowMinutes:60,\n  live:{ events:30, subs:14 200, avgRisk:48, highRisk:6 },\n  sample:[8 newest events] }
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : SimulationResultDto
SPA --> ANALYST : ✅ Simulation complete: 30 events persisted (SIM- prefix)\n6 HIGH-risk detected in anomaly pipeline reacted correctly

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 14 — Traffic Forecast (Capacity Planning)
' =====================================================================
== Phase 14 · Traffic Forecast (Capacity Planning) ==

ANALYST -> SPA : Forecast tab — next 6 hours

SPA -> GW  : GET /api/roaming/forecast?hoursAhead=6
GW  -> CTL : forward
CTL -> RIS : forecast(6)
RIS -> DB  : all events (incl. simulated)
DB  --> RIS : grouped by UTC hour
RIS -> RIS  : linear regression over hourly buckets\n  slope, intercept → 6 predicted points
RIS --> CTL : ForecastDto\n{ model:linear-regression, slope:+120/hr,\n  history:[{08:00,1420},{09:00,2310},{10:00,3180},...],\n  forecast:[{14:00,4200},{15:00,4320},{16:00,4440},\n            {17:00,4560},{18:00,4680},{19:00,4800}] }
CTL --> GW  : 200
GW  --> SPA : ForecastDto
SPA --> ANALYST : 📈 Upward trend: +120 subs/hr\nEvening peak ~4 800 subs at 19:00\n→ Flag to capacity team

' =====================================================================
'  PHASE 15 — Observability Drilldown (Grafana)
' =====================================================================
== Phase 15 · Observability Drilldown in Grafana ==

ANALYST -> GRAF : Open Grafana :3000

note over GRAF #FCE8E6
  All previous API calls generated:
  • Prometheus metrics  (http_server_requests_seconds_count, JVM metrics)
  • Loki logs           (Loki4j appender — structured JSON with traceId + spanId)
  • Tempo traces        (OTLP spans from Gateway OpenTelemetry Java Agent)
  • Service graph       (Tempo metrics_generator → Prometheus remote_write)
end note

ANALYST -> GRAF : Explore → Tempo → Service Graph (Node Graph)
GRAF --> ANALYST : Node graph: SPA → Gateway → RoamingService\ncall rate · error rate · latency P50/P95

ANALYST -> GRAF : Click on a slow trace (latencyP95 spike at 10:42)
GRAF --> ANALYST : Trace view: 9 spans\n  GW span: 412ms total\n  RoamingController: 389ms\n  RoamingInsightsService.analyzeCsv: 381ms\n  CsvParser.parse: 340ms (slowest — 342 rows)

ANALYST -> GRAF : Click "Logs for this span" (tracesToLogs drilldown)
GRAF --> ANALYST : Loki log lines for traceId=abc123:\n  INFO  CsvParser    — parsed 342 rows, skipped 4 (missing QoS cols)\n  WARN  AnomalyDetector — 11 anomalies above threshold\n  INFO  RoamingInsights — forecast slope=+74 subs/hr

ANALYST -> GRAF : Open Redis & Storage dashboard
GRAF --> ANALYST : Redis instances: 2 UP\nMemory used: ratelimit-redis 14MB · anomaly-redis 8MB\nKeyspace hit ratio: 94%

ANALYST -> GRAF : Open Spring Boot dashboard → roaming-analysis-service
GRAF --> ANALYST : HTTP requests: 38 req/session · avg 210ms\nJVM heap: 312MB / 512MB\nGC pauses: < 5ms

' =====================================================================
'  END — Summary
' =====================================================================
== End-of-Shift Summary ==

note over ANALYST, GRAF #E6F4EA
